.fill.justify.offset 5.rightmargin 55.pagesize 48.m1 2.m2 1.m3 2.m4 3.ec X.header /Sbatch/Network/Sbatch.footer /Page #//Printed (%)/.in +5.define topic.bold.in -5$1 $2 $3 $4 $5.in +5.en.define endtopic.en.define noform.nojustify.nofill.en.define noformend.justify.fill.en.! Manual created with MWB.! END-OF-MACRO.topic NAMESbatch - Collect and batch News article for remote system.endtopic.topic SYNOPSIS.noformsbatch [-c|-c7|-b|-s] [-f=<size>] <system>.noformend.endtopic.topic DESCRIPTION  Sbatch collects all article which should be send to a remote system.On default all articles are batched into one file until the size limitis reached. With.bold-cyou can compress the news to get a better throughput,.bold-c7will encode them after compression to transmit them over lines whichonly supports 7 Bit. With.bold-sall articles are spooled as single files..bold-f=<size>gives the limit of a file in kBytes. the default is 50 kByte..endtopic.topic CAVEATSThe files are stored in temporary on /dd. If this too small things mayfail..endtopic.topic BUGSMay be a lot, none known..endtopic.topic FILES.noform.noformend/h0/SPOOL/BATCH.in +3The articles are stored herein, for each system one file with thefilename of the system..in -3.noformend.endtopic.topic SYSINFO.noform.noformendNEWS.batch,s=/h0/SPOOL/BATCH.in +3the directory where the files for the systems are found..in -3.noformend.endtopic.topic SEE ALSOInews - in this distributiomRnews - in this distributiom.endtopic.topic AUTHOR.in 0.ce 5Ulrich DessauerKerschensteinerstr. 45, D-8034 GermeringVoice: +49 89 8417811E-Mail: ..!{chiuur|doitcr}!nitmar!udud@nitmar.ddt.sub.org.endtopic